{
  "uid": "urnetwork-extender-health",
  "title": "urnetwork / extender health",
  "tags": [
    "urnetwork",
    "extenders"
  ],
  "description": "Whether extender records reach clients through each channel, how many extenders there are and how fast they churn, the gossip mesh's capacity, links and memory, and provider fleets that leave together (monitor/SIGNALS.md §28, from factury/research/extender-health-2026-11-11.md). Alerts are the monitor's.",
  "editable": false,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "5m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-7d",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timezone": "",
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "env",
        "label": "env",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "warp-mimir"
        },
        "query": "label_values(urnetwork_stats_online_extenders, env)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "release to clients (SIGNALS.md §28.1, §28.2, §27.2)",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "gossip release coverage",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "warp-mimir"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "warp-mimir"
          },
          "expr": "max(urnetwork_stats_extender_gossip_extenders_24h{env=\"$env\",kind=\"record\"}) / max(urnetwork_stats_online_extenders{env=\"$env\"})",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "description": "The online extenders whose record the gossip service released in the last 24 hours, as a share of the online extenders. A record lives a day and the drip re-releases each before it expires, so a healthy share is about 100% (100-115% from 2026-10-30 to 11-06, counting extenders revoked during the day). 0% from 2026-11-07 to 11-11 22:15Z, when the drain was dead. The monitor warns under 50% for an hour (extender-release-coverage-low)."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "oldest unreleased gossip message",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "warp-mimir"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "warp-mimir"
          },
          "expr": "max(urnetwork_stats_extender_gossip_oldest_pending_seconds{env=\"$env\"})",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "description": "The age of the oldest record or revocation written to the gossip publish queue and not yet released. The gossip replicas drain the queue every 5 seconds, so a healthy value is seconds; 5.6 days on 2026-11-11. The monitor warns above 10 minutes (extender-gossip-stalled, SIGNALS.md §27.2)."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "stored activations (last hour)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "warp-mimir"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "warp-mimir"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(urnetwork_extender_activations_total{env=\"$env\",stage=\"store\",outcome=\"activated\"}[1h]))",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "description": "Extender activations the api stored in the last hour. Each answers its extender with its own fresh record and eight random peers. At least 7 an hour from 2026-11-03 to 11-11; the monitor warns at none for 90 minutes (extender-activations-stopped)."
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "extenders in dns",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "warp-mimir"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "warp-mimir"
          },
          "expr": "max(urnetwork_taskworker_extender_dns_extenders{env=\"$env\"})",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "description": "Distinct extenders behind the addresses the extender dns tick published. On a taskworker with the publish fix (SIGNALS.md §27.2) it counts only the sets Route 53 accepted; on an older one, the sets the tick wanted, which read 62 while every batch was refused from 2026-10-28. What clients are actually served is the monitor's extender-dns-records (§28.2)."
    },
